Category: branding
Summary: per-user system extensions folder on Windows is %APPDATA%\Remilia\Extensions, not LibreWolf's

Purpose: LibreWolf's mozilla-dirs.patch hard-codes "LibreWolf" as the parent
of the per-user system extensions folder (AppendSysUserExtensionPath). On
Windows that is %APPDATA%\LibreWolf\Extensions, so extensions that other
software installs there for LibreWolf would also be loaded by Remilia.
Files: toolkit/xre/nsXREDirProvider.cpp (XP_MACOSX || XP_WIN branch; the
string is shared with macOS, which Remilia does not target). The Unix branch
(".librewolf") is not changed: Linux is not a Remilia target.
Not changed on purpose: the macOS update root (XP_MACOSX branch of
GetUpdateRootDir); on Windows the update root comes from the install path.
Prefs touched: none.
Upstreamable: no (Remilia identity).
Reverting: Remilia uses %APPDATA%\LibreWolf\Extensions again.

--- a/toolkit/xre/nsXREDirProvider.cpp
+++ b/toolkit/xre/nsXREDirProvider.cpp
@@ -1304,7 +1304,7 @@
 
 #if defined(XP_MACOSX) || defined(XP_WIN)
 
-  static const char* const sXR = "LibreWolf";
+  static const char* const sXR = "Remilia";
   rv = aFile->AppendNative(nsDependentCString(sXR));
   NS_ENSURE_SUCCESS(rv, rv);
 
